# --- s023 Book I d.3 q.8 (begotten knowledge; the ontological status of intellection)
n("n425","s023-01","Octaua questio tertie distinctionis","la","commentary","No question with this title stands in the Vatican *Ordinatio* I d. 3. The material corresponds to Scotus's treatment of the *notitia genita* and of the category of intellection: *Ord.* I d. 3 nn. 600–604, the replies in the question on the image (actus secundi *sunt producti*; intellection as a form *in continua dependentia ad praesentiam suae causae*), and *Quodl.* q. 13. As with q. 7, Gorris's exemplar seems to have had a question here that the critical edition does not.","to-verify")
n("n426","s023-01","forme non est tantum generatio sed compositi","la","source","Arist. *Metaph.* VII 8, 1033b16–19: neither the form nor the essence is generated; the composite is.","certain")
n("n427","s023-01","Aug. de trini. 9. c. 12.","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* IX 12.18: *ab utroque enim notitia paritur, a cognoscente et cognito*.","certain")
n("n428","s023-02","substantia non adest et abest","la","source","Porphyry's definition of accident (*Isagoge*, c. 5): *accidens est quod adest et abest praeter subiecti corruptionem*.","certain")
n("n429","s023-02","Sed dicit quidam et clarius","la","commentary","The anonymous 'someone' who says 'more clearly' that intellection is an action not in the category of action but of quality. This is Scotus's own considered position (*Quodl.* q. 13 a. 2, and *Ord.* I d. 3 nn. 601–603). Gorris therefore seems to be contrasting the formulation of his source here with the clearer one found elsewhere in Scotus. It may also be Francis of Meyronnes or another Scotist.","to-verify")
n("n430","s023-02","Aristoteles. 6°. ethicorum","la","source","The distinction of immanent and transient action is in Arist. *Metaph.* IX 8, 1050a23–b2 (seeing and contemplating remain in the agent), not in *Ethics* VI, though *Eth.* VI 4, 1140a1–5 distinguishes making from doing. The citation is probably loose.","certain")
n("n431","s023-02","in questione venienti latius dicetur","la","commentary","The next question (s024 = *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 3 q. 2) treats the causes of intellection at length.","certain")
# --- B collation (full): B35R–B36L
upd("n427", append=" B: *Aug. de trini. ix. c. ix. et xi.* (the next line, at the top of B36L, begins *ca. ij.*, which is unclear). A's *c. 12* is correct.")
upd("n429", append=" B: *Sed dicit quidem et clarius*. B's *quidem* leaves the verb without its subject; A's *quidam* is right.")
